{"name":"Ferrous","hex":"#cc926c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ferrous","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or containing iron.","Of compounds of iron in which it has a valence or oxidation number of +2."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ferrous"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ferrous","blocks":[{"text":"In chemistry, iron(II) refers to the element iron in its +2 oxidation state. The adjective ferrous or the prefix ferro- is often used to specify such compounds, as in ferrous chloride for iron(II) chloride (FeCl2). The adjective ferric is used instead for iron(III) salts, containing the cation Fe3+. The word ferrous is derived from the Latin word ferrum, meaning \"iron\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Eisen%28II%29-chlorid-Tetrahydrat.jpg/330px-Eisen%28II%29-chlorid-Tetrahydrat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferrous","wikidata":"Q428946"},{"title":"Ferrous (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Ferrous is an Indian crime drama feature film written, directed and produced by writer/director Shaurya Singh under his banner Silver Rain Pictures in collaboration with Amrit Sinha of Tanay Films International. Ferrous was premiered at RTF 2018, an International Film Festival held at Lagos, Nigeria in July 2018, in front of a packed international audience where it was judged Best Foreign Film. The film was later adapted to become a series and premiered on OTT platform Ullu in Feb 2022."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferrous_(film)","wikidata":"Q48672793"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Iron%28II%29_oxide.jpg/500px-Iron%28II%29_oxide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Iron%28II%29_oxide.jpg/1280px-Iron%28II%29_oxide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par